  {
   "id": "255069912",
   "type": "page",
   "status": "historical",
   "title": "KIP-927: Improve the kafka-metadata-quorum output",
   "version": {
    "by": {
     "type": "known",
     "username": "fvaleri",
     "userKey": "ae84fb5e7da6acf7017f74e432920596",
     "profilePicture": {
      "path": "/confluence/images/icons/profilepics/default.svg",
      "width": 48,
      "height": 48,
      "isDefault": true
     },
     "displayName": "Federico Valeri",
     "_links": {
      "self": "https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/rest/api/user?key=ae84fb5e7da6acf7017f74e432920596"
     },
     "_expandable": {
      "status": ""
     }
    },
    "when": "2023-05-25T12:39:36.000Z",
    "message": "",
    "number": 13,
    "minorEdit": false,
    "hidden": false,
    "_links": {
     "self": "https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/rest/experimental/content/255069912/version/13"
    },
    "_expandable": {
     "content": "/rest/api/content/255069912?status=historical&version=13"
    }
   },
   "position": 920,
   "body": {
    "storage": {
     "value": "<p><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"toc\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:macro-id=\"9aac097e-9615-4079-a55c-3bfbb979b937\" /></p><h1>Status</h1><p><strong>Current state</strong>: <em>Accepted</em></p><p><strong>Discussion thread</strong>: <em><a href=\"https://lists.apache.org/thread/pph59hxvz5jkk709x53p44xrpdqwv8qc\">here</a><br /></em></p><p><strong>JIRA</strong>: <em><a href=\"https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-14982\">here</a><br /></em></p><p>Please keep the discussion on the mailing list rather than commenting on the wiki (wiki discussions get unwieldy fast).</p><h1>Motivation</h1><p>When running kafka-metadata-quorum script to get the quorum replication status, the LastFetchTimestamp and LastCaughtUpTimestamp output is not human-readable.</p><p>It would be convenient to add an optional flag to enable a human-readable format showing the operation delay in ms (i.e. 366 ms ago).</p><p>This delay is computed as (now - timestamp), where they are both represented as Unix time (UTC based).</p><h1>Public Interfaces</h1><p>A new optional flag called --human-readable will be added to the kafka-metadata-quorum tool.</p><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:macro-id=\"abe2e3a8-dfb0-4ac5-a1e3-c0532b5f8b14\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"language\">bash</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[$ bin/kafka-metadata-quorum.sh describe -h\nusage: kafka-metadata-quorum --bootstrap-server BOOTSTRAP_SERVER describe [-h] [--status] [--replication] [--human-readable]\n\noptional arguments:\n  -h, --help             show this help message and exit\n\nStatus:\n  --status               A short summary of the quorum status and the other provides detailed information about the status of replication.\n\nReplication:\n  --replication          Detailed information about the status of replication\n  --human-readable       Human-readable output]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro><h1>Proposed Changes</h1><p>The current default --replication output is as follows and will remain unchanged.</p><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:macro-id=\"2938d9aa-7349-4b15-b512-ff4e5a67946d\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"language\">bash</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[$ bin/kafka-metadata-quorum.sh --bootstrap-server :9092 describe --replication\nNodeId\tLogEndOffset\tLag\tLastFetchTimestamp\tLastCaughtUpTimestamp\tStatus  \t\n2     \t551         \t0  \t1683732558012     \t1683732558012        \tLeader  \t\n3     \t551         \t0  \t1683732557573     \t1683732557573        \tFollower\t\n4     \t551         \t0  \t1683732557573     \t1683732557573        \tFollower]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro><p><br /></p><p>Instead, when passing the new flag, we will have the following output (note how argparse4j support abbreviations).</p><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:macro-id=\"036177d9-71e9-447f-9eed-8969a648302d\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"language\">bash</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[$ bin/kafka-metadata-quorum.sh --bootstrap-server :9092 describe --replication --human-readable\nNodeId\tLogEndOffset\tLag\tLastFetchTimestamp\tLastCaughtUpTimestamp\tStatus  \t\n2     \t8689        \t0  \t4 ms ago          \t4 ms ago             \tLeader  \t\n3     \t8689        \t0  \t148 ms ago        \t148 ms ago           \tFollower\t\n4     \t8689        \t0  \t148 ms ago        \t148 ms ago           \tFollower\n\n$ bin/kafka-metadata-quorum.sh --boot :9092 describe --re --hu\nNodeId\tLogEndOffset\tLag\tLastFetchTimestamp\tLastCaughtUpTimestamp\tStatus  \t\n2     \t61          \t0  \t5 ms ago          \t5 ms ago             \tLeader  \t\n3     \t61          \t0  \t56 ms ago         \t56 ms ago            \tFollower\t\n4     \t61          \t0  \t56 ms ago         \t56 ms ago            \tFollower]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro><h1>Compatibility, Deprecation, and Migration Plan</h1><p>The default behavior will remain unchanged to avoid breaking any tool relying on the current timestamp output.</p><h1>Test Plan</h1><p>A new test method will be added to MetadataQuorumCommandTest to verify default and new behaviors with regard to the timestamp output.<em><br /></em></p><h1>Rejected Alternatives</h1><p>Using a date/time formatting (i.e. May 10, 15:54:55 UTC) won't add much information in most cases and you will have to deal with locale.<em><span><br /></span></em></p><p><br /></p>",
